<title>UK: Midland Ind up as old bid rumours resurface.</title>
<headline>Midland Ind up as old bid rumours resurface.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Midland Independent Newspapers Plc spiked higher on Tuesday as old rumours of a bid, possibly from Mirror Group Plc, resurfaced in the market, dealers said.</p>
<p>Midland shares were up 26-1/2p or 18 percent at 175 by 0837 GMT in active trade of 491,000 shares. MGN was down 1p at 207-1/2 in trade of 305,000.</p>
<p>&quot;Apparently the story does the rounds about once every six months,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>No-one at Midland Independent was immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
